15. Integrated Framework: OVI and OARF

15.1 Orbital Viability Index (OVI)
We formalise OVI as:

\text{OVI} = \frac{\bar{P}_{\text{solar}} \cdot \text{CCR} \cdot \mathcal{R}}{\bar{A}_{\text{rad}} \cdot L \cdot \mathcal{S}},
\tag{9}

where \bar{P}_{\text{solar}} is normalised available solar power, \mathcal{R} the reliability factor (mission success probability), \bar{A}_{\text{rad}} the normalised radiator area per FLOP, L launch cost, and \mathcal{S} systemic risk factor (probability of catastrophic loss). Normalisation is against a baseline: 1 MW SSO H100 system with solid radiators at current launch costs.

Table 2 shows OVI for candidate architectures:

Architecture OVI
Baseline (LEO, solid rad, H100) 1.0
SSO, droplet rad, H100 4.2
